{"id":"u-6234d0ee-f4b5-4c20-94d3-6f960fe7d220","src":"community","title":"GROK Custom Powerbuilding","author":"Jay M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/nmCaKW-grok-custom-powerbuilding","desc":"This is the Prompt I used to get this routine using Grok Heavy:\n\nI am a 47 year old male I am 5'11 260lbs and have a muscular physique. My body fat is around 19% and muscle weight is around 205lbs. I am taking 600mg of Sustanon a week and 400mg of Deca a week. Help me find a workout that will maximize strength and size. I have no constraints on time\n\nThe five-day powerbuilding split below is an effective program for maximizing both strength and hypertrophy, blending heavy compound lifts on \"power\" days with higher-volume accessory work on \"hypertrophy\" days. It's structured over 8 weeks, with progression built in via increasing sets, weights, and reps over time. This allows for progressive overload while leveraging your enhanced recovery (given your current regimen). Run it for 8 weeks, then reassess—deload if needed by reducing volume/load by 20-30% for a week.\n\nKey Guidelines\n\nWarm-up: Start each session with 5-10 minutes of light cardio (e.g., rowing or cycling) and dynamic stretches. Do 1-3 warm-up sets per exercise, ramping up to your working weight.\n\nRest Periods: 3-5 minutes on power days (focus on max effort); 60-90 seconds on hypertrophy days (keep the pump and tension high).\n\nProgression: Use reps in reserve (RIR)—leave 1-2 reps in the tank per set. Add weight when you hit the top of the rep range across all sets. If you stall, drop weight by 10% and build back up. Track everything in a log. Aim for controlled eccentrics (3-4 seconds lowering) on hypertrophy work.\n\nNutrition/Recovery: Eat in a surplus (e.g., 500 calories above maintenance) with high protein (1.6-2.2g per kg bodyweight). Prioritize sleep and mobility work.\n\nEquipment: Assumes access to a full gym (barbells, dumbbells, machines, cables).\n\nModifications: If an exercise aggravates something, swap (e.g., front squat for back squat if back issues). Start conservative on weights given your size—use 70-80% of 1RM for compounds initially.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-15T02:38:54.417Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper Body Power","Lower Body Power","Chest/Shoulders/Triceps Hypert","Lower Body Hypertrophy","Back/Biceps Hypertrophy"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":80,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Assisted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Military Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Decline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Alternating Dumbbell Curl","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Skull Crusher (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"pct":85,"x":4}]},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"pct":75,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Standing Calf Raise","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Barbell Ab Wheel","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Decline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Overhead Tricep Extension (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Stiff Leg Deadlift (Dumbbell)","se